WEBVTT

00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:14,670
What supplements do you recommend for kidneys? My urine, while fairly clear, is foamy?

00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:24,750
Why wouldn't make recommendations for your kidneys based upon the look of your urine?

00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:33,070
So urine can be foamy for multiple reasons. It can be foamy if a person is dehydrated,

00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:41,070
that can cause a little bit of foamy urine. It can be foamy based upon your stream. If your stream is

00:00:41,070 --> 00:00:49,950
quick, or if you're using a, if you're catheterized, it's very common to have foamy urine just because

00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:56,110
of how it's emptied into the bag. If you have a strong stream, you can have foamy urine and there's

00:00:56,110 --> 00:01:02,350
nothing wrong. This foamy, this of a urine is not diagnostic in itself. So I would say you don't

00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:09,310
base your supplements based upon that side, you would base your supplements based upon other

00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:17,550
things, whether it be a cheek swab tester, whether it be a blood test or toxicity test or whatever

00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:22,750
other testing you're doing some objective data that's based, that you're basing your choice on.

00:01:23,710 --> 00:01:29,870
So supplements that you'd recommend for the kidney, it's based upon what's going on with the

00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:39,790
kidneys and the foaminess of your urine really isn't telling me anything. So you'd, you'd analyze

00:01:39,790 --> 00:01:43,630
what's going on with your kidneys. You do that through different blood tests. You can tell what's

00:01:43,630 --> 00:01:51,630
going on with your kidneys, creatine levels, your BUN levels can give you indication that there's

00:01:51,630 --> 00:01:58,990
stress in the kidneys, symptoms like signs of kidney stones, CT scans, MRIs, things like that that

00:01:58,990 --> 00:02:06,590
you're giving us data that you're having some kidney failure or slow functioning of the kidneys.

00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:13,390
There's lots of different nutrients that could help with that. We would want to base it on that

00:02:13,390 --> 00:02:19,870
data. So I wouldn't say, it may be you're not saying this, but let's say you're saying, oh my

00:02:19,870 --> 00:02:31,150
urethus is fairly clear and foamy, what does that mean? Well it can mean nothing so we'd have

00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:37,790
to get more data. So if you know you have kidney issues then we'd want to take that data and make

00:02:37,790 --> 00:02:41,230
a decision on supplements. So there's a lot of different choices for this

